{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"Multi-row/low-wave tiles cut the short-width kernels by as much as 3×. The next safe algebraic optimization is to omit max subtraction: softcapping bounds every logit to ±30, so unshifted exponentials cannot overflow in float32, and the normalized result is mathematically identical. I’m testing the resulting change in rounding against all tolerances before adopting it."}}
