{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"agent_message","text":"The sequential-row variant does not improve the long-row path, and the existing 2048 configuration remains best. One worthwhile shape-generic optimization remains for ragged widths: 691 currently pays for 1024 exponentials per row and 293 pays for 512. I’m testing split power-of-two chunks (512+256 and 256+64) so only a small tail is masked."}}
